WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.494
Django extracts and
renders messages,

2
00:00:03.494 --> 00:00:06.000
and translators fill
in each PO file.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:10.795
Django does its part well: it
marks strings anywhere and formats

4
00:00:10.795 --> 00:00:12.106
dates per locale.

5
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.785
General Translation
fills Django's PO files,

6
00:00:15.785 --> 00:00:17.607
plural forms included,

7
00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:18.651
with your terms.

8
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.880
Keep running makemessages,

9
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.642
and point the gt config
at your locale folders.

10
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.620
Then npx gt translate fills every
language before compilemessages

11
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.675
runs in CI.

12
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.646
A Glossary keeps terms consistent,

13
00:00:33.646 --> 00:00:36.826
and reviewers can edit each
entry in the Dashboard.

14
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.099
Your team now ships
Russian with each release.
